<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Persis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Persis is the Greek name for the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pars">Pars</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>, in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> it was ruled by local kings. Its ruler Ardashir exploited Parthian weakness to defeat the last Parthian king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artabanus-iv">Artabanus IV</a>, in 224 CE, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/persis.jpg" alt="Persis" width="320" height="146" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Persis_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
